{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins","id":688884,"title":"Other shifters origins","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-04T15:15:58-07:00","id":688884,"title":"Other shifters origins","content":"If we assume that other shapeshifter races works mostly like Uratha - just like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688070-arindhal-the-wind-lords\">fan created <b>Arindhal</b>, wereeagles</a> - what could there in setting be origins of those werebeasts kinds?<br /> <br /> Uratha are said to be children of Luna and Wolf, Arindhal to be sired by Helios and Gaia. What could be origins of Coyote, Spider and Crow Folk?<br /> <br /> I'm mostly interested in possible origins of werebears, as they are mine faves. I spose they would be related more to Gaia than Luna, but do not know other spirit with the pair - only Bear? Arindhal skipped animal spirits part by equaling Helios with Eagle, so maybe Gaia=Mother Bear then?<br /> <br /> Bonus: Male Hishu forms for werebears could look like this...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/aeQUxBt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Yes, I'm bi bear - I wrote it few times on forums. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-04-2015, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T16:10:59-07:00","id":688981,"title":"","content":"My headcanon was always just that Luna kind of got around. Every animal is affected by the Moon's phases to some extent. The reason that Werewolves are Luna's favorite is because Werewolves (and canines more broadly) have a very strong symbolic connection to the Moon.<br /> <br /> So there could be dozens of Father spirits, for each brood of shapeshifters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T22:28:29-07:00","id":689317,"title":"","content":"On one hand it's logical that Luna, goddess of change, would be mother of <b>all</b> shapeshifters. It would make nice explanation why shifters have always five forms ( like Lunas Phases ), why they shapeshift from human to animal ( Luna is said to walk as human on the Earth ) and why they are weak on silver.<br /> <br /> But then we got in to family ties, and things start to look weird (even for Goddes of Change and Madness ) - if Luna is sister to both Helios and Gaia, then their &quot;sacred breeds&quot; ( let's assume eagles and bears for now ) could not be blessed by their patrons. They would be Luna + Eagle and Luna + Bear children, that's a bit contrary to &quot;fluff&quot;, with Eagles being blessed by Helios and Bears being specials of Gaia. And <b>all</b> shifters would be weak to silver. A bit boring, I must say.<br /> <br /> All that Luna + Helios or Luna + Gaia could not bare their children - spirit children would be then spirits of celestial objects, not half flesh hybrids. Not to talk about inscest in this way of thinning...<br /> <br /> What I would think more logical in this paradigm would be that<i> werewolves were first of their shapeshifting kind.</i> O<i>ther Shadow Gods wanted they own offspring / guardians when Pangaea were more and more going to the end</i>. They used Uratha &quot;blue prints&quot; and made their own modifications by siring half flesh spirits hybrids with animal spirits. In that way all shapeshifters technically are cousins, even if partially created from Uratha and descend from them.<br /> <br /> If we would go this route, I would assume by 2ED rules that each Breed needs their version of Auspices, but not need to be connected to Moon Phases. For example, in werebear as Children of Gaia and Bear, I would rather make their version of Auspices connected to the place <b>where</b> they First Change took place, not when - Water, Forest, Cave, Mountain. ( Need one more... ) In modern cities the analogs would work. It's logical for the half spirits of Earth itself, does it not?<br /> <br /> Still, even then I do not have idea on Bears Bane, like Silver is for wolves or Gold for Eagles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T23:10:44-07:00","id":689353,"title":"","content":"All I know is that it'd be cool to have weremantises. Yes, that's right. Weremantises. I'm not really sure how it'd work, but the Thri-Kreen-like war form alone would be worth it. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T23:18:41-07:00","id":689355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689353#post689353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is that it'd be cool to have weremantises. Yes, that's right. Weremantises. I'm not really sure how it'd work, but the Thri-Kreen-like war form alone would be worth it. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Gythka</i> and <i>chatkcha </i>confirmed for <i>Hurt Locker</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T02:36:00-07:00","id":689513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689317#post689317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that Luna + Helios or Luna + Gaia could not bare their children - spirit children would be then spirits of celestial objects, not half flesh hybrids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Father Wolf was allegedly a spirit as well, so the issue of spirits having half-flesh children applies anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, even then I do not have idea on Bears Bane, like Silver is for wolves or Gold for Eagles. </div> </div> </div>Bronze (the first artificial material, thus symbolically outside Gaia's purview).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T03:11:15-07:00","id":689526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689513#post689513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Father Wolf was allegedly a spirit as well, so the issue of spirits having half-flesh children applies anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is difference from &quot;we have shapeshifitng animal-cosmological hybrid spirit&quot; than &quot;we are unreflected cosmological spirits&quot; - both are unleashed, but we know that Uratha are human hybrids of Wolf and Luna spirits, not only Wolf ones. Not without reasons Uratha have Auspices and can work sometimes as practical Lunes.<br /> <br /> Two Celestial Body would create Celestial spirit, not Animal-Celestial hybrid that Uratha have as their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689513#post689513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bronze (the first artificial material, thus symbolically outside Gaia's purview).</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool, stealing this to the Children of Gaia Breeds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689353#post689353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is that it'd be cool to have weremantises. Yes, that's right. Weremantises. I'm not really sure how it'd work, but the Thri-Kreen-like war form alone would be worth it. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Just think with what would Mantis spirits most intermingle - Earth, Moon or Sun - and we could make them fan reality. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-05-2015, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T05:02:16-07:00","id":689580,"title":"","content":"I see Luna as more of a patron for shapechangers, not necessarily the creator of all of them. In the books she's only involved with a few of them, and things like Father Wolf 'get around' more often, with at least eight Firstborn to their name and possibly several more.<br /> <br /> I really don't like a zoo of shapechangers, especially ones that are just werewolves with a different animal. Werewolves aren't wolf-spirits, they're part spirits of the hunt, and the wolf was just the major representation of that. Having every other animal have a similar shapechanger misses the meaning behind werewolves. It's worth noting that even the 'Wayward Sons' from War Against the Pure just have three forms, human, hybrid and animal. Near-forms are only gained with Aspect points. Skinchangers goes even further away from the standard werewolf shifter.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't mind Pangaeans as an origin for shapechangers, I just think using it as the sole origin for all them is sort of lazy and lessens the concept as a whole.<br /> <br /> If you want a spirit bear as an origin there's the Great Bear from Hunting Ground: Rockies. Between its story and the sample bans for bears in Predators it looks like losing those it protects seems to knock the wind out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T06:16:08-07:00","id":689626,"title":"","content":"Below I shown mine theory about origins of various animal shapeshifters, like Uratha.<br /> <br /> <b>Impossible Children</b><br /> Uratha, werewolves, are children of Luna and Wolf. They are impossible creature, having inside them human flesh, wolf and moon spirit parts. And they are perfect predators.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why Shadow Gods become envy of Moon and Wolf of their progeny. Ideal hunters they were, Uratha were only of their like. Sun and Earth felt threatened, even if Uratha were children of their sister. Legends say that even other Celestial Spirits were afraid of werewolves.<br /> <br /> Soon both Helios and Gaia saw that Uratha are changing subtle balance in Pangea. They needed their shapeshifting Impossible Children. And so the Changing Breeds come to life\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b><br /> From rules standpoint, Uratha and rest of their distant cousins share the same mechanics. Minor differences are marked in their text. Most crucial one is that each shapeshifting Breed is coming from one Animal and one Celestial parent \u2013 just like Uratha are coming from Wolf and Moon. This legacy is marked by werewolves weakness to silver, Moon Metal \u2013 called often as Bane Metal. The same \u201csacred metals\u201d are associated with others Celestial Parents, remarkably good mirrored in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classical_planet#Alchemy\" target=\"_blank\">humans alchemy associations</a> between Celestial Bodies and Bane Metals. They Celestial Parent also determine variant of Auspices faction the Breed have.<br /> <br /> Here is list of Celestial Parents to the the Metal Bane they carry on to shapeshifters:<ul><li>The Sun - Gold</li> <li>The Moon - Silver</li> <li>Earth \u2013 Bronze \u2013 not pure metal, as all were created in the Gaia itself, but this artificial alloy is potent symbol of weakness to the Gaia, still burning her Impossible Children.</li> </ul>Possible other shapeshifters can come from rarer Celestial Parents.<ul><li>Mercury - Quicksilver</li> <li>Venus - Copper</li> <li>Mars - Iron</li> <li>Jupiter - Tin</li> <li>Saturn - Lead</li> </ul><b>Common Breeds</b><br /> Even most typical Impossible Children are rare \u2013 much more than Uratha. Werewolves were first and most successful of their cousins. But small societies to the other Celestial and Animal pairs were formed and thrived, that werewolves meet from time to time. Here is not finite list, rather guidance of what can be possible in the particular setting.<br /> <br /> <b>Sun </b>\u2013 Auspice variants are based on the Day Phases ( see Exalted )<ul><li>Eagles \u2013 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688070-arindhal-the-wind-lords\">Arindhal</a></li> <li>Lions</li> <li>Bulls</li> </ul><b>Moon \u2013 </b>Auspice variants are based on the Moon Phases ( like with Uratha )<ul><li>Wolves</li> <li>Egyptian cats</li> <li>House cats</li> </ul><b>Earth</b> \u2013 Auspices are variants of elements or locations First Change take place<ul><li>Bears</li> <li>Insects ( like Mantis )</li> <li>Stags</li> </ul>So what you think about all of this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-05-2015, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T06:20:52-07:00","id":689631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689580#post689580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see Luna as more of a patron for shapechangers, not necessarily the creator of all of them. In the books she's only involved with a few of them, and things like Father Wolf 'get around' more often, with at least eight Firstborn to their name and possibly several more.<br /> <br /> I really don't like a zoo of shapechangers, especially ones that are just werewolves with a different animal. Werewolves aren't wolf-spirits, they're part spirits of the hunt, and the wolf was just the major representation of that. Having every other animal have a similar shapechanger misses the meaning behind werewolves. It's worth noting that even the 'Wayward Sons' from War Against the Pure just have three forms, human, hybrid and animal. Near-forms are only gained with Aspect points. Skinchangers goes even further away from the standard werewolf shifter.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't mind Pangaeans as an origin for shapechangers, I just think using it as the sole origin for all them is sort of lazy and lessens the concept as a whole.<br /> <br /> If you want a spirit bear as an origin there's the Great Bear from Hunting Ground: Rockies. Between its story and the sample bans for bears in Predators it looks like losing those it protects seems to knock the wind out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I <i><b>liked</b></i> 1ED <b>Changing Breeds</b>, even with wonky mechanics - most of ideas were made &quot;Breed-by-Breed&quot; cases, and they only vaguely think about they are connected to Nature. Problem was mechanics were too similar ( beside astronomical Forms stats changes ) and every shapeshifter felt as &quot;Uratha lesser&quot; - they even all shared the same Bane Metal, Silver! Not enough differences between the Breeds in some cases.<br /> <br /> I'm torn on this, as on one hand I would want the shifters with good mechanics - like using Werewolf Renown and Forms changes - but on the other making everyone the descended of Celestial and Animals spirits sounds a bit like <b>Exalted</b>, not <b>World of Darkness</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-05-2015, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T06:23:01-07:00","id":689632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689317#post689317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Water, Forest, Cave, Mountain. ( Need one more... )</div> </div> </div> </div>Plains? (or Swamp/Island, but those are both kinda covered by Water)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T07:32:23-07:00","id":689687,"title":"","content":"I am eager for Dark Eras to come out because the Neolithic chapter will shed a bit more light on how things worked back then with the Uratha etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T07:38:07-07:00","id":689690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=688981#post688981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My headcanon was always just that Luna kind of got around. Every animal is affected by the Moon's phases to some extent. The reason that Werewolves are Luna's favorite is because Werewolves (and canines more broadly) have a very strong symbolic connection to the Moon.<br /> <br /> So there could be dozens of Father spirits, for each brood of shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong way round - the reason that the Warden Moon and Great Predator bonded was that they were both vastly powerful boundary gods, nothing to do with anything animal.\u200b The reason wolves have a very strong symbolic connection to the Moon is probably *because* of that bonding in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T08:48:09-07:00","id":689764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689632#post689632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plains? (or Swamp/Island, but those are both kinda covered by Water)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going by the habitats Bears are known to take. I do not know if any Bear really lives in Plains...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T08:52:20-07:00","id":689765,"title":"","content":"I think that his Bane Metal...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689513#post689513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bronze (the first artificial material, thus symbolically outside Gaia's purview).<br /> <br /> Can really works with that idea...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689687#post689687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am eager for Dark Eras to come out because the Neolithic chapter will shed a bit more light on how things worked back then with the Uratha etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>... seeing as how Neolithic Age - and by this Sundering of Pangea - ended with invention of Bronze - alloy that kill Gaia's Children, like werebears. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:13:37-07:00","id":689778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689317#post689317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one hand it's logical that Luna, goddess of change, would be mother of <b>all</b> shapeshifters. It would make nice explanation why shifters have always five forms ( like Lunas Phases ), why they shapeshift from human to animal ( Luna is said to walk as human on the Earth ) and why they are weak on silver.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why werewolves are 'part' human is something that werewolves question as well, given the apparent origin of Luna and Wolf - both spirits. The reason for werewolves having human shape is not because of any claimed form of a human that Luna ever took, and indeed it's not very likely she *did* ever take a human form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Luna is sister to both Helios and Gaia </div> </div> </div> Worth noting that Gaia is a purely hypothetical entity that quite possibly doesn't exist. Helios, for its part, is a very, very long way away from Earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And <b>all</b> shifters would be weak to silver. A bit boring, I must say. </div> </div> </div> I seem to remember that the other shifters in War against the Pure are not vulnerable to silver, but may be misremembering. Azlu and Beshilu have no Bane weaknesses at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I would think more logical in this paradigm would be that<i> werewolves were first of their shapeshifting kind.</i> </div> </div> </div> Werewolves origins, and the Great Predator's unique relationship with the Border Marches, are things that will be discussed in the Neolithic Era. Even by then, though, a lot of what the Uratha believe about their origins was already conjecture.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:23:46-07:00","id":689790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689778#post689778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves origins, and the Great Predator's unique relationship with the Border Marches, are things that will be discussed in the Neolithic Era. Even by then, though, a lot of what the Uratha believe about their origins was already conjecture.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As well it should be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:29:14-07:00","id":689795,"title":"","content":"<b>Cahalith archaeologist investigating ancient Uratha ruins: </b>&quot;What the hell is a '<i>Lunar Exalted</i>'?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:29:23-07:00","id":689796,"title":"","content":"So... how about were-cetaceans? Remaking the brineborn so to speak.<br /> <br /> For all Life came from the Oceans, to there it must return. So to, then must some of the land dwellers reclaim their ancestral homeland.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Although, that said, I can't seem to get the idea out that they'd have things resembling psychic powers as the default...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Didn't someone make wereotters at one point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:32:36-07:00","id":689799,"title":"","content":"I actually tried designing weredolphins once for a one-shot game that never got off the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:38:10-07:00","id":689826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689799#post689799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually tried designing weredolphins once for a one-shot game that never got off the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I've got a few projects on the back burner right now, so I can offer to help within the current week. Want to start a thread?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, funny thought, what if T4 werebeasts <i>become</i> effectively Lunar Exalted","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:47:17-07:00","id":689835,"title":"","content":"Oh, that was years ago. I don't even live in the same city as the group I was planning that for any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:53:35-07:00","id":689838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689795#post689795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Cahalith archaeologist investigating ancient Uratha ruins: </b>&quot;What the hell is a '<i>Lunar Exalted</i>'?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Exalted</b> was sold as possible mythical prehistory of <i>both</i> WoD settings. Yeah, Lunar and Solar Exalted sounds like Luna and Helios possible shapeshifting Children. This is why Shadow Gods of <b>Werewolf </b>look so much as the <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/CelestialBureaucracy\" target=\"_blank\">Celestial Buracracy</a> of setting. Hell, see the top of it on Exalted Wikia:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Wikia on Celestial Buracracy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The Celestial Incarna</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The celestial incarna are the most powerful of the gods.</span></span><ul><li>The <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/UnconqueredSun\" target=\"_blank\">Unconquered Sun</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Luna\" target=\"_blank\">Luna</a></li> <li>The <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/FiveMaidens\" target=\"_blank\">Five Maidens</a>:<ul><li><a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Mercury\" target=\"_blank\">Mercury</a>, the Maiden of Journeys</li> <li><a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Venus\" target=\"_blank\">Venus</a>, the Maiden of Serenity</li> <li><a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Mars\" target=\"_blank\">Mars</a>, the Maiden of Battles</li> <li><a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Jupiter\" target=\"_blank\">Jupiter</a>, the Maiden of Secrets</li> <li><a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Saturn\" target=\"_blank\">Saturn</a>, the Maiden of Endings</li> </ul></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Some in Creation consider <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Gaia\" target=\"_blank\">Gaia</a> one of the Celestial Incarna, though this is technically incorrect, as she is one of the <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Primordials\" target=\"_blank\">primordials</a>. (see <i>Games of Divinity</i>, pg. 8)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Helios, Luna and Gaia as one of most powerfull beings in whole Creation, hello?<br /> <br /> It looks like nWoD is Exalted setting after dozen of Exarchs timelines editions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689826#post689826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, funny thought, what if T4 werebeasts <i>become</i> effectively Lunar Exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>Could elobrate? I do not get this point. Maybe mine English is too bad to get this statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-05-2015, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T10:00:27-07:00","id":689845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689796#post689796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... how about were-cetaceans? Remaking the brineborn so to speak.<br /> <br /> For all Life came from the Oceans, to there it must return. So to, then must some of the land dwellers reclaim their ancestral homeland.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Although, that said, I can't seem to get the idea out that they'd have things resembling psychic powers as the default...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Didn't someone make wereotters at one point?</div> </div> </div> </div> All good ideas! As for the Wereotters, that was Leliel, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/15828-new-shifter-kushtaka-the-trickster-wereotters\">here.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T10:23:23-07:00","id":689884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689778#post689778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why werewolves are 'part' human is something that werewolves question as well, given the apparent origin of Luna and Wolf - both spirits. The reason for werewolves having human shape is not because of any claimed form of a human that Luna ever took, and indeed it's not very likely she *did* ever take a human form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we have an rumor that Uratha comes from some Wolf-Moon Idigam merged with human body. And this is still the idea I come from, even if it is not necessarily sure answer. But some setting and mechanics assumptions need to be done decide <i>how</i> other shapeshifters would work in-setting. &quot;They have similar origins to Uratha, only fron other Shadow Gods&quot; is a still better answer than what 1ED <b>Changing Breeds</b> or <b>War with The Pure</b> gave us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689778#post689778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth noting that Gaia is a purely hypothetical entity that quite possibly doesn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>This why we have &quot;Nature&quot; answer in the <b>Changing Breeds </b>- that means <i>exactly</i> the same as Gaia. But so developed societies of shapeshiters monsters need some kind of common origin and their connection to Shadow begs to point their patron is some kind of &quot;Spirit God&quot; - putting two and two together - Shapeshifters are close to being the proof of Gaia-as-spirit theory as one can be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689778#post689778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Helios, for its part, is a very, very long way away from Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>And still he <i>bombards</i> the Earth's Shadow with his Helions every second of the day. <b>Werewolf</b> 2ED even goes one whole page on Helios actions on the Earth's Shadow, like the unnecessary guard that all the times looks to it's far reached territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: The Forsaken 2ED</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>THE MOON, SUN, AND WOLF</b><br /> The current in the Gauntlet during the day and the effect of Shadow-sunlight have the same cause. While Luna is ever-changing and protean, guarding the earthly Shadow from alien void spirits, her brother Helios is steadfast, unchanging, and pushes everything within the lunar sphere \u201cin,\u201d forcing Essence to ground, fixing spirits in place and creating the Shadow\u2019s \u201cgravity.\u201d Werewolves who convince aerial spirits to carry them into the sky discover that they can\u2019t reach the moon no matter how hard they try \u2014 the increasing pressure of Helios\u2019 solar winds force them back long before they reach the void.<br /> <br /> Ithaeur who\u2019ve dealt with Helions know all too well that Helios hasn\u2019t forgiven the Forsaken as his sister has. Mostly, it\u2019s because it\u2019s not in Helios\u2019 nature to change his mind about anything, but partly, it\u2019s because of the Sundering. Just as Luna gives the Hisil its ever-changing, reactive nature, Helios provides the impetus for spirits attempting to leave. By his nature, he forces everything away. Before his death, Father Wolf hunted the spirits fleeing the Shadow, complementing both Luna and her brother. By killing him, the first pack destroyed that harmony, and made Helios the unwitting cause of the material world\u2019s woes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Helios can be far away, but he always mingle in the Earth's Shadow. I just conclude that he would want to have his 'agents'/Children ( in the form of shapeshifters ) in Material world also, to guard Shadow on all fronts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689778#post689778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to remember that the other shifters in War against the Pure are not vulnerable to silver, but may be misremembering.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <b>War Against the Pure </b>makes Silver the Bane of <i>all </i>shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>War Against the Pure</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver<br /> In regards to regeneration, pure silver harms shapechangers exactly as it does the Forsaken (see p.169, Werewolf: The Forsaken). This surprises those werewolves who discover the weakness, as the Uratha tie their silver vulnerability to legends surrounding the death of Urfarah and the curse of Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's boring answer, as we have there marked Helios chosen Distant Ones, for example - if they are marked by Helios, not the Luna, why do they all are weak to Silver, not Gold?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689778#post689778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Azlu and Beshilu have no Bane weaknesses at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hosts are <i><b>not</b></i> shapeshifters, even if there is theory that Uratha evolved from the Father Wolf's Host. I think that Celestial Parent of Luna makes this evolution possible - or diffrent. At least from books, it seams, that only Human-Animal Spirits hybrids would be rather Hosts, than true shapeshifters. Celestial Parent ( mostly Luna ) is need to make them <i>more</i> than Host of their Animal side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689778#post689778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves origins, and the Great Predator's unique relationship with the Border Marches, are things that will be discussed in the Neolithic Era. Even by then, though, a lot of what the Uratha believe about their origins was already conjecture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really cannot wait to read it! ( And compare mine theories <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-05-2015, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T11:02:49-07:00","id":689916,"title":"","content":"Going by the second edition core, it looks like werewolves take human form so they can hunt among humans, one of the more dominant and widespread species. I'd also point out that humans are one of the greatest hunter species, though we stopped relying on it long ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-05-2015, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T14:07:49-07:00","id":690381,"title":"","content":"By the Exalted reference, I meant that werewolf/werebeast archmage equivalents would have powers quite similar in effect and range as Lunar exalted, the T4 equivalent game, if you will.<br /> <br /> Still, Wyrd, have you considered less... celestial beings to drop upon for patrons and parents? Consider in my example I cited the Oceans for weredolphins. You can reasonably do the same with massive biome spirits, such as the Amazon Rainforest, the Himalayan mountain range, all of Antartica?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T15:16:36-07:00","id":690483,"title":"","content":"Well, most of my homebrewed Breeds had some basis in ancient mythology. The more Amerindian breeds, like the Were-Rattlers and Gila-men, were easy enough, as both Nahuali have established legends, as did most of the other Breeds I wrote (having roles in classic myths, however minor, is a plus, hence the Were-ants and Were-Crabs). The Were-Jellies were the hardest to justify, as I could find only 1 myth related to jellyfish, and it wasn't very well represented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T15:50:49-07:00","id":690532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=690381#post690381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the Exalted reference, I meant that werewolf/werebeast archmage equivalents would have powers quite similar in effect and range as Lunar exalted, the T4 equivalent game, if you will.<br /> <br /> Still, Wyrd, have you considered less... celestial beings to drop upon for patrons and parents? Consider in my example I cited the Oceans for weredolphins. You can reasonably do the same with massive biome spirits, such as the Amazon Rainforest, the Himalayan mountain range, all of Antartica?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, basically any rank 7 or above spirit could reasonably spawn its own line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T16:51:37-07:00","id":690605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=690483#post690483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, most of my homebrewed Breeds had some basis in ancient mythology. The more Amerindian breeds, like the Were-Rattlers and Gila-men, were easy enough, as both Nahuali have established legends, as did most of the other Breeds I wrote (having roles in classic myths, however minor, is a plus, hence the Were-ants and Were-Crabs). The Were-Jellies were the hardest to justify, as I could find only 1 myth related to jellyfish, and it wasn't very well represented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me if this is a bit forward, but could you provide links or directions to these myths? Sorry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T05:56:08-07:00","id":691116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=689580#post689580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like a zoo of shapechangers, especially ones that are just werewolves with a different animal. Werewolves aren't wolf-spirits, they're part spirits of the hunt, and the wolf was just the major representation of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with one caveat. Either go for one whole hog and have a completely different setup for different kinds of shapeshifter. Or go for the other whole hog, and redefine Father Wolf as Father Hunter, and the Uratha as shapeshifters into predatory animals rather than wolves specifically.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T10:48:46-07:00","id":691434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688884-other-shifters-origins?p=690605#post690605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this is a bit forward, but could you provide links or directions to these myths? Sorry!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_worship\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_worship</a> provided a good starting point for most of what I wrote, as did the pages for each of the different animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}